      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-2859",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/a7/a7f84e5ae5a86c0da6b1de1e3f8b957972179f3510b146a9144632b801923ba7.png)\n\nThe height of a conical paper cup is $10cm$ and the base radius is $30cm$. The cup is being filled with water so that the water level, $h$, rises at a rate of $\\frac{2}{h}cm/s$. At what rate is the volume of water in the cup increasing when the water level is $7cm$?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
