      ":question/problem": "![](images/ee/ee000fd6fbacce3ca200588517e81e698bd7c3c436efc625f8ef079cec6e3133.png)\n\nA conical tank has a height of $4m$ and the radius at the bottom of the tank is $3m$. Some solution is leaking from the tank through a small hole. If the solution level is decreasing at a rate of $2m/h$, find the rate at which the volume of the solution is decreasing when the solution level is $2m$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
